+/*
+ * ISHTAR ADSP (SM8550): the audio DSP started through TrustZone PAS, and its battery manager read over GLINK.
+ * On this phone the charger (PM8550B) and the fuel gauge belong to the ADSP's charger_pd: the stock kernel only asks
+ * it (stock DT /soc/qcom,pmic_glink, channel PMIC_RTR_ADSP_APPS; HyperOS qti_battery_charger). There is no gauge the
+ * application processor can read by itself. The values go to iokit/Kernel/arm/IshtarBattery.cpp.
+ *
+ * Boot-arg ishtar-adsp=1: take over the DSP that UEFI started (uefi-ishtar uefipil.cfg [AUTO] FULL_ADSP); proven on the
+ * phone. ishtar-adsp=2: if UEFI did not start it, load it here (TZ PAS below), which still hangs the SoC in MEM_SETUP of
+ * the dtb image (pas 36). Off by default. All logs start with "ISHTAR ADSP:".
+ * Bring-up: ishtar-adsp-step=N stops before step N+1; ishtar-adsp-delay=S waits S seconds after the firmware is
+ * found (default 10); every step line is followed by a 500 ms pause so it reaches the
+ * USB live log before a possible hang.
+ *
+ * Firmware: HyperOS /vendor/firmware_mnt/image/{adsp,adsp_dtb}.{mdt,bNN} (the modem partition's production-signed
+ * copy, what HyperOS's remoteproc loaded), pushed to /private/var/ishtar/adsp/ (scripts/push.py).
+ *
+ * Sequence (Linux qcom_q6v5_pas.c adsp_load/adsp_start, sm8550 resource: pas 1, dtb pas 36, proxy lcx+lmx,
+ * load_state "adsp"):
+ *   dtb: INIT_IMAGE(36, .mdt), MEM_SETUP(36), copy segments    (adsp_load)
+ *   our SMP2P item 429 ("master-kernel"), as Linux smp2p does at probe
+ *   AOP "load_state adsp on", RPMh lcx/lmx at level 384, AUTH_AND_RESET(36)
+ *   main: INIT_IMAGE(1, .mdt), MEM_SETUP(1), copy segments, AUTH_AND_RESET(1)
+ *   wait for "slave-kernel" ready (bit 1); give the rails back on handover (bit 2)
+ *   GLINK over SMEM (items 478/479 ours, 480 the DSP's), version, channels IPCRTR and PMIC_RTR_ADSP_APPS
+ *   QRTR hello + the service registry locator (pd-mapper: QMI service 64), then battmgr property gets every 10 s
+ *
+ * Addresses (stock/ishtar/ishtar-merged.dts): remoteproc-adsp@3000000 (memory-region adspslpi 0x9ea00000+0x4680000,
+ * q6_adsp_dtb 0x9e980000+0x80000), smem 0x81d00000+0x200000 (hwlock tcsr_mutex 3 = 0x1f43000), qcom,smp2p-adsp
+ * (smem 443/429, pids 0/2, ipcc client 3 signal 2), glink-edge (ipcc client 3 signal 0), ipcc@408000, aoss_qmp
+ * @c300000 (ipcc client 0), apps_rsc drv-2 0x17a20000 tcs-offset 0xd00 (ACTIVE TCS 0..2, RSC v3 layout as
+ * ishtar_touch.c rh8_send), cmd-db 0x81c60000. PD domains from the firmware's *.jsn (instance 74).
+ * Protocols: Linux qcom_smem.c, smp2p.c, qcom_glink_native.c / qcom_glink_smem.c, net/qrtr/ns.c, qcom_pd_mapper.c,
+ * qmp mailbox (qcom_aoss.c), downstream qti_battery_charger.c property ids.
+ *
+ * ponytail: polled, no IPCC interrupt (20 ms idle, 1 ms while waiting for an answer); one thread owns everything.
+ * ponytail: the RPMh TCS is shared with ishtar_touch.c without a lock: touch votes at boot, this after root mount.
+ * ponytail: the DSP is never stopped; a reboot resets it (XBL).
+ */
